/** @page imagemagickreleasenotesguide Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section imagemagick_v1_0 imagemagick Module Version 1.0
    - initial release
    - a font that names a file is refused with \c PERMISSION-DENIED by
      @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage::annotate() "MagickImage::annotate()" and
      @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickDrawing::setFont() "MagickDrawing::setFont()" if the calling code is restricted
      from the file system, and the file-system policy of a sandbox that governs the code applies to it
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-imagemagick/issues/8">issue 8</a>)
    - a font or font family with a quote, a backslash or a control character is refused, as it would add commands to
      the drawing script; for code that a sandbox governs, a file name with a coder prefix, a list file or a
      \c "[...]" suffix is refused, and for restricted or sandboxed code an explicit read format whose data can name
      other files (such as \c MVG, \c SVG, \c MSL or \c TEXT) is refused
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-imagemagick/issues/8">issue 8</a>)
    - the file paths, the fonts that name files and the image data in formats that name other files that the methods
      of @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage "MagickImage" and @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickDrawing "MagickDrawing"
      take are refused with \c PERMISSION-DENIED for the restricted code that a host-created object of a module class
      was given to, as the object's methods run with the file system lent (see @ref imagemagickcallerpaths and
      @ref Qore::ImageMagick::IM_LENT_PATH_CHECKS,
      <a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-imagemagick/issues/10">issue 10</a>)
    - the file operations of @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage "MagickImage" check the file-system policy of the
      sandbox that governs the code that calls them; they checked that of the code that created the image, so an
      image that the host created read and wrote any file for sandboxed code
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-imagemagick/issues/11">issue 11</a>)
*/
